WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.640
Data mining is the process of extracting valuable&nbsp;
information from large data sets, patterns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.440
trends, insights, that you can help to understand&nbsp;
your business better, and there are four stages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.080
The first of those is setting objectives. This is&nbsp;
where data scientists and business stakeholders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.280
work together to define a business problem that&nbsp;
data mining will be applied too. Step two is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:25.200
when we take a look at data preparation this is&nbsp;
identifying the data that we need to help answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.320
these questions and then cleaning that data to&nbsp;
remove any noise such as duplicates missing values&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.880
and outliers. Then three, this is the interesting&nbsp;
part this is where we take a look at a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:40.320
algorithms and this is things like clustering&nbsp;
association classification and deep learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:46.400
to derive data relationships. And then finally&nbsp;
four brings us to results where we interpret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.840
these results to make sure that they are valid,&nbsp;
novel, useful, and understandable. data mining

